    <bpmn:process id="W_W1295" name="W1295. New Store Opening Readiness, Systems Go-Live &amp; Staff Training Validation" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: New store construction substantially complete; target opening date confirmed
Frequency: 10–15 new store openings per year
Volume: 1 store opening per event; typically clustered in Q1 and Q3
Owner: Store Opening Project Manager
Participants: Store Opening PM, Store Manager (designate), IT, HR, Merchandising, Supply Chain, Marketing, VP Store Operations
Source: workflow W1295 — New Store Opening Readiness, Systems Go-Live &amp; Staff Training Validation</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1295_LaneSet7">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1295_Lane1" name="Store Opening PM">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1295_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1295_Task14</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1295_Task16</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1295_Start8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1295_Lane2" name="IT Team">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1295_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1295_Lane3" name="HR">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1295_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1295_Lane4" name="Compliance">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1295_Task12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1295_Lane5" name="Supply Chain">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1295_Task13</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1295_Lane6" name="Marketing">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1295_Task15</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1295_End17</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1295_Start8" name="New store construction substantially complete; target opening date confirmed">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1295_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1295_Task9" name="Opening readiness kickoff (T-12 weeks)">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Opening readiness kickoff (T-12 weeks): Store Opening PM conducts kickoff with all functional leads: (a) confirm target opening date, (b) assign readiness owners: IT (systems), HR (staffing), Merchandising (stock plan), Supply Chain (initial replenishment), Marketing (grand opening campaign), Compliance (permits), (c) establish weekly status meeting cadence, (d) create readiness tracker with milestones and RAG status per functional area
Responsible (R): Store Opening PM
Accountable (A): VP Store Operations
Duration: 4 hours</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1295_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1295_Flow21</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1295_Task10" name="Systems installation &amp; configuration (T-10 weeks)">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Systems installation &amp; configuration (T-10 weeks): IT team installs and configures store systems: (a) network infrastructure (WiFi, LAN, POS network), (b) POS terminals (3 units) with offline capability tested, (c) handheld devices (receiving tablets, stock counting RF guns), (d) CCTV system per W405 with recording and remote monitoring, (e) biometric attendance system per W10, (f) back-office PC and printer, (g) systems integration test: POS ↔ ERP data flow, inventory sync, price download, loyalty system
Responsible (R): IT Team
Accountable (A): CIO
Duration: 2 weeks</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1295_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1295_Flow22</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1295_Task11" name="Staff hiring &amp; training (T-8 weeks)">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Staff hiring &amp; training (T-8 weeks): HR executes store staffing plan: (a) hire Store Manager and Assistant Store Manager (T-8 weeks — earliest), (b) hire remaining 27 staff (Department Supervisors, Sales Associates, Cashiers, Receiving Clerks, Stock Associates, Customer Service, Maintenance) by T-6 weeks, (c) conduct 2-week training program: POS operation per W518, product knowledge by department, safety orientation per W440, receiving procedures per W1283, customer service standards per W13, ERP system basics (inventory lookup, price check, customer lookup), (d) all Cashiers must pass POS competency certification per W518 before opening
Responsible (R): HR / Store Manager
Accountable (A): CHRO
Duration: 6 weeks</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1295_Flow22</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1295_Flow23</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1295_Task12" name="Permits &amp; compliance (T-8 weeks)">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Permits &amp; compliance (T-8 weeks): Compliance team ensures all regulatory requirements met: (a) BIR POS registration and CAS registration per W216 — critical path, as BIR processing can take 4–6 weeks, (b) LGU business permit per W54 for new location, (c) BFP fire safety inspection certificate per W476, (d) DENR environmental compliance certificate if required, (e) local barangay clearance, (f) sign permit for exterior signage, (g) verify all permits posted in-store as required by law
Responsible (R): Compliance
Accountable (A): VP Legal
Duration: 4–8 weeks</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1295_Flow23</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1295_Flow24</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1295_Task13" name="Initial stock delivery &amp; merchandising (T-4 weeks)">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Initial stock delivery &amp; merchandising (T-4 weeks): Supply Chain and Merchandising execute initial stocking: (a) supply planning generates initial stock order per W2A based on planogram and expected demand for new market, (b) DC schedules consolidated initial stock delivery (typically 3–4 truckloads over 2 weeks), (c) Merchandising team executes planogram: shelf layout, price tags, promotional displays, category signage, (d) initial consignment stock from vendors per W23 if applicable, (e) store markdown team sets opening promotional pricing per W262
Responsible (R): Supply Chain / Merchandising
Accountable (A): VP Merchandising
Duration: 3–4 weeks</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1295_Flow24</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1295_Flow25</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1295_Task14" name="Soft opening &amp; systems stress test (T-1 week)">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: Soft opening &amp; systems stress test (T-1 week): Conduct 2–3 day soft opening: (a) invite employees&#x27; families and friends for live transaction testing, (b) stress test all 3 POS terminals simultaneously, (c) test offline POS capability by simulating network outage, (d) test receiving with a practice delivery, (e) test ecommerce BOPIS flow with test orders, (f) identify and resolve any systems or process issues before public opening
Responsible (R): Store Opening PM / IT
Accountable (A): VP Store Operations
Duration: 3 days</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1295_Flow25</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1295_Flow26</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1295_Task15" name="Grand opening execution (T-0)">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 7: Grand opening execution (T-0): Marketing executes grand opening per W14: (a) official ribbon-cutting with local LGU officials and community leaders, (b) opening day promotional pricing and loyalty sign-up drive, (c) media coverage (local radio, social media), (d) vendor demonstration events per W1289 for opening weekend, (e) full staff deployment with Store Opening PM on-site for issue escalation, (f) IT on standby for any system issues
Responsible (R): Marketing / Store Manager
Accountable (A): VP Store Operations
Duration: 1–2 days</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1295_Flow26</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1295_Flow27</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1295_Task16" name="Post-opening stabilization (T+1 to T+4 weeks)">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 8: Post-opening stabilization (T+1 to T+4 weeks): Store Opening PM monitors new store performance for 4 weeks: (a) daily sales vs. target, (b) POS system uptime and error logs, (c) inventory accuracy after initial selling period, (d) staff performance and training gaps, (e) customer feedback, (f) supply chain replenishment on-time rate, (g) weekly status report to VP Store Operations; hand off to Store Manager and Regional Manager at T+4 weeks
Responsible (R): Store Opening PM / Store Manager
Accountable (A): VP Store Operations
Duration: 4 weeks</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1295_Flow27</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1295_Flow28</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1295_End17" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1295_Flow28</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1295_Annotation18">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-218 (ensure facility compliance &amp; lease-cost integrity.) | - operational: standard operating procedures; system-enforced validation rules
Owner: Store Opening Project Manager</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W1295_Assoc19" sourceRef="W1295_Annotation18" targetRef="W1295_Start8" associationDirection="None" />
