    <bpmn:process id="W_W1427" name="W1427. Store Expansion Pipeline Management, Site Readiness Milestone Tracking &amp; Go-Live Checklist" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Annual expansion plan approval by CEO/Board (typically Q4 for next year&#x27;s pipeline); or new site identification by Real Estate team
Frequency: 10–15 new stores/year; pipeline managed continuously with monthly status reviews
Volume: ~10–15 active store construction projects at any time (staggered: 2–3 in site selection, 3–5 in construction, 3–5 in pre-opening preparation)
Owner: VP Store Operations
Participants: VP Store Operations, Real Estate Manager, Construction Manager, Store Manager (designee), IT Project Manager, HR Recruitment Manager, VP Merchandising, Supply Planning Manager, VP Legal, Regulatory Compliance Officer
Source: workflow W1427 — Store Expansion Pipeline Management, Site Readiness Milestone Tracking &amp; Go-Live Checklist</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1427_LaneSet2">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1427_Lane1" name="VP Store Operations">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1427_Task4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1427_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1427_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1427_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1427_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1427_Start3</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1427_End9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1427_Start3" name="Annual expansion plan approval by CEO/Board (typically Q4 for next year&#x27;s pipeline); or…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1427_Flow12</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1427_Task4" name="Annual pipeline planning">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Annual pipeline planning (Q4): VP Store Operations presents next year&#x27;s expansion plan to CEO/Board: (a) target: 10–15 new stores, (b) priority regions based on market analysis (population density, competitor presence, construction activity), (c) capital budget: 10–15 stores × PHP 30–50M per store = PHP 300–750M capex, (d) timeline: staggered openings across Q1–Q4 to manage resource allocation, (e) Board approves annual expansion plan and capex budget
Responsible (R): VP Store Operations
Accountable (A): CEO / Board
Duration: 2–3 weeks</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1427_Flow12</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1427_Flow13</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1427_Task5" name="Pipeline milestone tracking">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Pipeline milestone tracking (ongoing): VP Store Operations maintains pipeline dashboard with milestones per project: (a) Phase 1 — Site Selection: site identified → LOI signed → due diligence complete → lease executed, (b) Phase 2 — Design &amp; Permitting: architectural design → LGU building permit → BIR registration → fire safety permit, (c) Phase 3 — Construction: groundbreaking → structural completion → MEP (mechanical/electrical/plumbing) → interior fit-out → fixture installation → punch list, (d) Phase 4 — Pre-Opening: IT infrastructure installed → POS configured → staff hired and trained → merchandise loaded (W1415) → LGU business permit obtained (W1421) → dry run, (e) Phase 5 — Go-Live: final inspection → opening day
Responsible (R): VP Store Operations / Construction Manager
Accountable (A): COO
Duration: 2–3 hours/week (pipeline review)</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1427_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1427_Flow14</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1427_Task6" name="Weekly project status meeting">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Weekly project status meeting: VP Store Operations chairs weekly expansion pipeline meeting with all workstream leads: (a) Construction Manager: construction progress vs. timeline, issues (weather delays, contractor performance, material delivery), (b) IT Project Manager: POS, network, RF guns, CCTV installation status, (c) HR Recruitment Manager: store team hiring progress (29 positions per store), (d) Supply Planning Manager: merchandise loading plan per W1415, (e) Regulatory Compliance Officer: permit status per W1421, (f) identify blockers: any workstream that may delay go-live → escalate with mitigation plan
Responsible (R): VP Store Operations
Accountable (A): COO
Duration: 1–2 hours/week</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1427_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1427_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1427_Task7" name="Go-live readiness checklist">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Go-live readiness checklist (T-2 weeks): VP Store Operations conducts go-live readiness assessment per store: (a) Construction: 100% complete, punch list items resolved, certificate of occupancy obtained, (b) IT: POS terminals operational, network connectivity verified, offline capability tested per W535, (c) Staffing: all 29 positions filled, training completed (POS, safety, product knowledge per W518), (d) Merchandise: initial stock build complete per W1415, planogram compliance verified per W86, (e) Permits: LGU business permit posted per W1421, BIR POS registration confirmed, fire safety certificate posted per W1051, (f) Marketing: grand opening promotion planned per W14.1, local advertising launched, (g) score each area Green (ready) / Yellow (minor issues — can resolve before opening) / Red (blocking — cannot open); all areas must be Green or Yellow to proceed
Responsible (R): VP Store Operations
Accountable (A): COO
Duration: 4–8 hours/store</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1427_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1427_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1427_Task8" name="Post-opening 30-day review">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Post-opening 30-day review: VP Store Operations reviews new store performance at 30 days post-opening: (a) sales vs. plan (daily flash per W1419), (b) customer traffic vs. projection, (c) operational issues identified in first 30 days, (d) staff performance and customer feedback, (e) lessons learned for next store in pipeline
Responsible (R): VP Store Operations
Accountable (A): CEO
Duration: 2–3 hours/store</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1427_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1427_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1427_End9" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1427_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1427_Annotation10">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-302 (ensure controlled execution — Engineering &amp; Construction (PA-20.2).) | - operational: VP Store Operations review and approval gate
Owner: VP Store Operations</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W1427_Assoc11" sourceRef="W1427_Annotation10" targetRef="W1427_Start3" associationDirection="None" />
